course: dictionary
lesson: 11077
title: Welfare: health, safety and help
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Welfare is a word about looking after someone well. It means how healthy, happy and safe a person or an animal is. «Some people eat meat; vegetarians and vegans do not, for reasons of animal welfare, health, the environment or religion.» Here welfare is about how animals are treated. The words around it are the clues: animal welfare sits next to health and the environment, so it is about caring for animals.
explain: Welfare has a second meaning, about help from the government. «Welfare is government help for people who need it.» If you read «on welfare» or a sentence about money for people who are poor, ill or old, the word means help given by the state. Ask yourself: is the sentence about being well and safe, or about help given by the government? The surrounding words tell you which.
explain: Look for the phrases, too. «Child welfare», «the welfare of» and «animal welfare» all mean care for someone's health, happiness and safety. «Zoos test whether enrichment works... this is part of animal welfare science.» Scientists check animal welfare by watching what animals do, such as pacing, playing and resting.
fact: Welfare means the health, happiness and safety of a person or animal.
fact: «Welfare» can also mean help, often money, that the government gives to people who need it.
fact: «Animal welfare» means treating animals kindly and caring for their needs: food, water, shelter, health and freedom from fear.
fact: «Hurting animals on purpose is cruelty; tell a trusted adult, who can report it to an animal welfare organisation.»
fact: «Pacing» means walking the same path again and again, often a sign of boredom or stress in an animal.
exercise: «Animal welfare» means treating animals kindly and caring for their needs. What does it mean? | *Treating animals kindly and caring for their needs | A kind of animal food | Hurting animals on purpose | Animals that are very big
exercise: «Welfare is government help for people who need it.» In this sentence, what is welfare? | The safety of a playground | *Help, often money, given by the government to people who need it | A word for a hospital | A type of holiday
exercise: «Zoos test whether enrichment works by counting behaviour such as pacing, play and resting.» Find and copy the one word that can be a sign of boredom or stress. | resting | counting | *pacing | play
test: Mia says, «The vet checked the puppy's welfare.» What is the vet checking? | How much money the puppy costs | The colour of the puppy's coat | How many toys the puppy has | *How well the puppy is doing: its health, happiness and safety
test: The text says some people do not eat meat. Which reason does it give? | Because they like the colour of vegetables | To get help from the government | Because meat is too expensive | *Animal welfare, health, the environment or religion
exam: Read «a trusted adult, who can report it to an animal welfare organisation». What does an animal welfare organisation most likely work for? | Collecting money for the government | Selling animals in shops | Running a school for children | *Looking after the health, safety and needs of animals
